 ('An apparently safe pointer races with destruction', 'std::atomic<Node*> head;\nNode *read() { return head.load(); }\nvoid replace(Node *next) { delete head.exchange(next); }', 'Atomic head access is race-free but a concurrent reader can use a deleted object.', 'Define lifetime reclamation and memory-order assumptions independently.', 'Atomic raw-pointer operations do not provide ownership or safe reclamation.'),
